## Tag `weights`: every checkpoint key, accounted for

**What it is for.** The target loads this checkpoint: each key is loaded,
transformed, shared out across ranks, or deliberately skipped with the
reason written beside it.

**Hand back.** The weight-loading code and its test, in the files your card
names; mapping, transformation and sharding stay in that code. No forward
and no routing.

**How it is judged.** Your test reads the checkpoint as data (its index and
its config) and holds the mapping to its keys; it loads no engine. A loader
that asserts every tensor was consumed must know the ones it skips. Names
to search: `load_weights`, `post_load_weights`, and the quantization this
checkpoint states.
